["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A black tail near Harrison is not a big animal. One accurate, expanding load, zeroed and practised, does the job. A drawer of mixed boxes does not.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 342\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Match three stamps before you load: 1 the calibre stamped on the side of the barrel, .308 Win; 2 the headstamp on the base of each cartridge, .308 WIN; 3 the label on the box. All three must say .308 Winchester.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"342\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Match 3 stamps before you load</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"42\" width=\"376\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"62\" width=\"250\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#C9D0C6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"155\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">.308 WIN</text><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"74\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">barrel</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"114\" width=\"376\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"166\" r=\"42\" fill=\"#C9A54A\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"166\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#C9D0C6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">MAKER</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"202\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">.308 WIN</text><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"166\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">headstamp</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"226\" width=\"376\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"240\" width=\"180\" height=\"38\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">308 Win 150 gr</text><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"258\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"263\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">box</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"300\" width=\"380\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"320.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">All 3 must say .308 Winchester.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Barrel, headstamp and box all say .308 Winchester <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Expanding hunting bullets only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Matching the cartridge, Tikka's own ammunition rules, the legal bullet, bullet types, picking one load, energy and the black tail, and storing ammunition.</li><li>Deeper lessons: <a href=\"#/s/cartridge-anatomy/0\">How a cartridge works</a>, <a href=\"#/s/ammo-guide/0\">Ammo for your guns</a>, <a href=\"#/s/ballistics-308/0\">.308 ballistics</a>, <a href=\"#/s/shot-placement/0\">Shot placement</a>.</li><li>Previous: <a href=\"#/s/mc-tikka-05\">Positions and drills</a>. Next: <a href=\"#/s/mc-tikka-07\">Cleaning and the bolt</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 342\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Match three stamps before you load: 1 the calibre stamped on the side of the barrel, .308 Win; 2 the headstamp on the base of each cartridge, .308 WIN; 3 the label on the box. All three must say .308 Winchester.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"342\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Match 3 stamps before you load</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"42\" width=\"376\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"62\" width=\"250\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#C9D0C6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"155\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">.308 WIN</text><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"74\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">barrel</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"114\" width=\"376\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"166\" r=\"42\" fill=\"#C9A54A\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"166\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#C9D0C6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">MAKER</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"202\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">.308 WIN</text><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"166\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">headstamp</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"226\" width=\"376\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"240\" width=\"180\" height=\"38\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">308 Win 150 gr</text><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"258\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"263\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">box</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"300\" width=\"380\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"320.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">All 3 must say .308 Winchester.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>The calibre is marked on the side of the barrel <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Headstamp and box must match it <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why it matters</summary><ul><li>\"The caliber designation for your rifle is marked on the side of the barrel\" (95%, Tikka manual page 9). \"Be certain that each round you use is in the proper calibre\" (95%, page 6).</li><li>7.62x39 (your SKS round) does not belong anywhere near the Tikka. Keep each rifle's ammunition in its own labelled box (Tip).</li><li>.308 Winchester and 7.62x51 NATO are close but not the same: use what your barrel says (Tip; the manual says use the right calibre, 95%). <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> with a gunsmith before shooting any 7.62x51.</li><li>Headstamp: <a href=\"#/s/cartridge-anatomy/0\">How a cartridge works</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 344\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The Tikka manual&#x27;s ammunition rules: 1 factory new ammunition made to CIP or SAAMI standards; 2 the right calibre, .308 Winchester; 3 inspect every round for splits, dents and defects; 4 nothing over 10 years old; 5, in orange, never shoot steel jacketed bullets; 6 test that the rifle runs reliably with it before buying a large batch. Reloaded ammunition voids the warranty.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"344\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Tikka&#x27;s ammunition rules</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"42\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"60\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Factory new, made to CIP or SAAMI</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"84\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"102\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Right calibre: .308 Win</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"126\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"144\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Inspect every round</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"168\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"186\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"191\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"191\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nothing over 10 years old</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"210\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"228\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Never steel jacketed bullets</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"252\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"270\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"275\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"275\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Test it in your rifle before a big buy</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"298\" width=\"376\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Reloads void the Tikka warranty.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Factory new, CIP or SAAMI, inspected, under 10 years old <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Never steel jacketed bullets <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the manual's words</summary><ul><li>\"Use only high quality, commercially manufactured ammunition that is manufactured in accordance with C.I.P. ... or SAAMI ... standards\" (95%, Tikka manual page 9). CIP is the European proof commission; SAAMI is the Sporting Arms and Ammunition Manufacturers' Institute.</li><li>\"Carefully inspect each cartridge before it is loaded in the magazine. Be certain the cartridge cases are not split, deformed, or the cartridges do not possess any other dents or defects (this applies even to factory ammunition)\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>\"Do not fire old (age over 10 years) ammunition in this firearm\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>\"DO NOT ever shoot with steel jacketed bullets!\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>\"Before purchasing a large batch, make sure that the rifle functions reliably with it\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>\"The use of reloaded, handloaded, remanufactured or other non standard ammunition voids all warranties\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 304\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four bullets cut in half. 1 soft point, cup and core: a copper jacket over a lead core. 2 bonded: the lead core is bonded to the jacket so it holds together. 3 all copper, lead free, with a hollow nose. 4 full metal jacket, crossed out in orange: it does not expand and it is unlawful to hunt with. 1 to 3 expand and are legal for deer.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"304\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunting bullets, cut in half</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"42\" width=\"92\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M43 146 L43 100 Q45 82 50 78 L62 78 Q67 82 69 100 L69 146Z\" fill=\"#B8733A\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M47 142 L47 96 Q56 70 65 96 L65 142Z\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\"/><path d=\"M50 78 Q56 68 62 78Z\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Soft point</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cup, core</text><rect x=\"106\" y=\"42\" width=\"92\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M139 146 L139 100 Q141 82 146 78 L158 78 Q163 82 165 100 L165 146Z\" fill=\"#B8733A\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M143 142 L143 96 Q152 70 161 96 L161 142Z\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\"/><path d=\"M146 78 Q152 68 158 78Z\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M143 142 L143 96 Q152 70 161 96 L161 142\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bonded</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">glued core</text><rect x=\"202\" y=\"42\" width=\"92\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M235 146 L235 100 Q236 76 248 70 Q260 76 261 100 L261 146Z\" fill=\"#B8733A\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M245 74 L248 102 L251 74Z\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><circle cx=\"218\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"218\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"248\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">All copper</text><text x=\"248\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">lead free</text><rect x=\"298\" y=\"42\" width=\"92\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M331 146 L331 100 Q332 76 344 70 Q356 76 357 100 L357 146Z\" fill=\"#B8733A\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M336 142 L336 102 Q344 80 352 102 L352 142Z\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\"/><circle cx=\"314\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"314\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"344\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Full metal</text><text x=\"344\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">jacket</text><line x1=\"314\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"374\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"374\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"314\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"222\" width=\"376\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">1 to 3 expand: legal for deer.</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">4 does not expand: unlawful to hunt with.</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Grey = lead core. Copper = jacket.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Full metal jacket and other non expanding bullets: unlawful to hunt with <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Soft point, bonded or all copper: legal <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the rule word for word</summary><aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout law\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">The rule</div><p>\"It is unlawful to hunt or trap with a rifle using a full metal jacketed non-expanding bullet, or a tracer, incendiary, or explosive bullet.\"</p></aside><ul><li>Source: BC synopsis, as quoted in <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/0\">Rule Book: legal methods</a> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Deer may be hunted with a centrefire rifle; your .308 qualifies (99%, page 13 table, via the Rule Book).</li><li>Your hunting area rules (MUs, Management Units, seasons, no shooting areas near Mission and Harrison): <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2/0\">Region 2</a>.</li><li>Bullet types (85%, <a href=\"#/s/cartridge-anatomy/0\">How a cartridge works</a>): cup and core soft points expand fast and are cheap; bonded bullets hold together through bone; all copper bullets are lead free and penetrate deep.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 338\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pick one load in four steps: 1 buy one box each of two loads with 150 to 165 grain hunting bullets; 2 shoot three groups of three at 100 metres from the bench with a cool barrel; 3 keep the load that groups tighter and feeds and ejects cleanly; 4 buy three to four boxes from the same lot, zero with it and hunt with it. Change loads and you must zero again.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"338\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pick one load in 4 steps</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"42\" width=\"376\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"69\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Buy 1 box each of 2 loads</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">150 to 165 gr hunting bullets</text><line x1=\"34\" y1=\"96\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"99.2\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M34 104 L31.4 98.6 L36.6 98.6z\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"104\" width=\"376\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"131\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">3 groups of 3 at 100 m</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">from the bench, cool barrel</text><line x1=\"34\" y1=\"158\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"161.2\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M34 166 L31.4 160.6 L36.6 160.6z\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"166\" width=\"376\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"193\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"189\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Keep the tighter, reliable one</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">it must feed and eject clean</text><line x1=\"34\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"223.2\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M34 228 L31.4 222.6 L36.6 222.6z\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"228\" width=\"376\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"255\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"251\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Buy 3 to 4 boxes, same lot</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">zero with it, hunt with it</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"292\" width=\"376\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Change loads? Zero again.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>150 to 165 gr expanding bullets suit black tails <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>One load, one zero <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: choosing for a black tail</summary><ul><li>Black tailed bucks weigh about 48 to 90 kg, does 40 to 65 kg (90%, BC deer account, via the <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-01\">mule deer Masterclass</a>).</li><li>A 150 gr cup and core soft point is plenty for deer (65%, <a href=\"#/s/ammo-guide/0\">ammo guide</a>). A 165 gr bonded bullet is a good all round choice if you may meet a black bear <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Your 1 in 10 twist suits 150 to 180 gr hunting bullets (65%, <a href=\"#/s/rifle-mechanics/0\">How a rifle works</a>).</li><li>Your 20 inch barrel is about 80 to 100 fps (feet per second) slower than the box, which is tested from a longer barrel (70%, <a href=\"#/s/ballistics-308/0\">.308 ballistics</a>).</li><li>Every load hits a different spot. Switch loads and you must zero again <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Write the load name and lot number on your zero card (Tip). Chapter 10 has the card.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout lean\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>My lean: buy one box of a 150 gr soft point and one of a 165 gr bonded load. Shoot both at the range day. Keep the one that groups best and feeds cleanly. Buy 3 more boxes of the same lot.</p></aside></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 362\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Energy of a 150 grain .308 load: 3,590 joules at the muzzle, 2,840 at 100 m, 2,210 at 200 m, 1,700 at 300 m. An orange dashed line marks the 1,356 joule, 1,000 foot pound, rule of thumb. All bars stay above it to 300 m. A black tailed buck weighs 48 to 90 kg. Your limit is your skill, not energy.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"362\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">150 gr .308 energy vs distance</text><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"70\" width=\"54\" height=\"180\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"101\" y=\"64.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3,590 J</text><text x=\"101\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0 m</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"108\" width=\"54\" height=\"142\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"177\" y=\"102.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2,840 J</text><text x=\"177\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 m</text><rect x=\"226\" y=\"140\" width=\"54\" height=\"110\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"253\" y=\"133.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2,210 J</text><text x=\"253\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">200 m</text><rect x=\"302\" y=\"165\" width=\"54\" height=\"85\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"329\" y=\"159.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1,700 J</text><text x=\"329\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">300 m</text><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"182\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 4\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">J</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"280\" width=\"376\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Orange line: 1,356 J (1,000 ft lb) rule.</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"322\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Black tail buck: 48 to 90 kg.</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"342\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Your limit is your skill, not energy.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A 150 gr load carries over 1,356 J (1,000 ft lb) past 300 m <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Your skill sets the limit, not the energy <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the numbers</summary><ul><li>Federal Power Shok 150 gr from the <a href=\"#/s/ballistics-308/0\">.308 ballistics</a> lesson: 3,590 J at the muzzle, 2,840 J at 100 m, 2,210 J at 200 m, 1,700 J at 300 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The 1,000 ft lb rule is a rule of thumb with no clear origin <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>A good bullet through both lungs matters more than energy (70%, <a href=\"#/s/shot-placement/0\">shot placement</a>). The deer vital zone with a margin is about 20 to 25 cm <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Your real limit: the plate test in <a href=\"#/s/mc-tikka-05\">chapter 5</a> (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 344\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The Tikka manual&#x27;s ammunition rules: 1 factory new ammunition made to CIP or SAAMI standards; 2 the right calibre, .308 Winchester; 3 inspect every round for splits, dents and defects; 4 nothing over 10 years old; 5, in orange, never shoot steel jacketed bullets; 6 test that the rifle runs reliably with it before buying a large batch. Reloaded ammunition voids the warranty.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"344\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Tikka&#x27;s ammunition rules</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"42\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"60\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Factory new, made to CIP or SAAMI</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"84\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"102\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Right calibre: .308 Win</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"126\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"144\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Inspect every round</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"168\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"186\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"191\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"191\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nothing over 10 years old</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"210\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"228\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Never steel jacketed bullets</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"252\" width=\"376\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"270\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"275\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"275\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Test it in your rifle before a big buy</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"298\" width=\"376\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Reloads void the Tikka warranty.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Locked, separate from the rifle <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Dry, cool, in its box (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: storage and the field</summary><ul><li>Tikka: store the ammunition in a separate locked location (95%, Tikka manual pages 5 and 8). The storage law is in <a href=\"#/s/mc-tikka-08\">chapter 8</a>.</li><li>Keep rounds in their box with the lot number. Loose rounds in a wet pocket corrode and pick up grit (Tip).</li><li>On the hunt: one loaded magazine in the rifle when you are set up, a few spare rounds in a closed pocket (Tip). No live ammunition in an attached magazine in a vehicle (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts/0\">Rule Book: unlawful acts</a>).</li><li>Lead warning: wash your hands after handling ammunition and after cleaning (95%, Tikka manual page 6, rule 12).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 304\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four bullets cut in half. 1 soft point, cup and core: a copper jacket over a lead core. 2 bonded: the lead core is bonded to the jacket so it holds together. 3 all copper, lead free, with a hollow nose. 4 full metal jacket, crossed out in orange: it does not expand and it is unlawful to hunt with. 1 to 3 expand and are legal for deer.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"304\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunting bullets, cut in half</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"42\" width=\"92\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M43 146 L43 100 Q45 82 50 78 L62 78 Q67 82 69 100 L69 146Z\" fill=\"#B8733A\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M47 142 L47 96 Q56 70 65 96 L65 142Z\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\"/><path d=\"M50 78 Q56 68 62 78Z\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Soft point</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cup, core</text><rect x=\"106\" y=\"42\" width=\"92\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M139 146 L139 100 Q141 82 146 78 L158 78 Q163 82 165 100 L165 146Z\" fill=\"#B8733A\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M143 142 L143 96 Q152 70 161 96 L161 142Z\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\"/><path d=\"M146 78 Q152 68 158 78Z\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M143 142 L143 96 Q152 70 161 96 L161 142\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bonded</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">glued core</text><rect x=\"202\" y=\"42\" width=\"92\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M235 146 L235 100 Q236 76 248 70 Q260 76 261 100 L261 146Z\" fill=\"#B8733A\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M245 74 L248 102 L251 74Z\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><circle cx=\"218\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"218\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"248\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">All copper</text><text x=\"248\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">lead free</text><rect x=\"298\" y=\"42\" width=\"92\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M331 146 L331 100 Q332 76 344 70 Q356 76 357 100 L357 146Z\" fill=\"#B8733A\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M336 142 L336 102 Q344 80 352 102 L352 142Z\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\"/><circle cx=\"314\" cy=\"60\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"314\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"344\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Full metal</text><text x=\"344\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">jacket</text><line x1=\"314\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"374\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"374\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"314\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"222\" width=\"376\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">1 to 3 expand: legal for deer.</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">4 does not expand: unlawful to hunt with.</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Grey = lead core. Copper = jacket.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>\"Three stamps, one name.\"</strong> Barrel, headstamp, box.</li><li><strong>\"It must open up.\"</strong> Expanding bullets only.</li><li><strong>\"One load, one zero.\"</strong></li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: mistakes, rule and the field task</summary><ul><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion): \"Buy one load by the case, not ten loads by the box.\"</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Mixing loads in a pocket and missing because the zero moved.</li><li>Shooting old surplus or steel jacketed bullets in the Tikka.</li><li>Taking full metal jacket \"practice\" rounds on the hunt.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Before the range day: buy the two test loads, write their names and lot numbers in the journal, and check every round for dents and split necks.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>Tikka manual <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. BC synopsis via the Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Hunt Mentor lessons for loads and energy (65 to 90%). Checked 2026-10-23.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://media.sako.global/image/upload/v1691658741/Tikka_T1x_T3x_Instruction_Manual_v5.3_cjggnu.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tikka T1x and T3x instruction manual v5.3 (PDF)</a>: basic safety rules 3, 7 and 12 (pages 5 and 6), ammunition (page 9). Read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li><a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/0\">Rule Book: legal methods</a> (expanding bullets, page 13 weapons table) and <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts/0\">unlawful acts</a>, 2 October 2026 synopsis edition <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li>Hunt Mentor: <a href=\"#/s/ammo-guide/0\">ammo guide</a>, <a href=\"#/s/ballistics-308/0\">.308 ballistics</a> (Federal load data), <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-01\">mule deer Masterclass</a> (black tail weights), <a href=\"#/s/shot-placement/0\">shot placement</a></li></ul></details>"]